WEBVTT

00:12.150 --> 00:14.530
Where am I?

00:15.360 --> 00:17.030
Hey, wake up.

00:17.200 --> 00:19.160
I can't eat anymore.

00:19.160 --> 00:20.830
Quit that cliché sleepy talk!

00:20.910 --> 00:23.120
Huh? Where are we?

00:23.120 --> 00:25.500
I think we were brought here
while we were sleeping.

00:25.830 --> 00:28.130
I don't even remember falling asleep.

00:28.460 --> 00:30.500
And what the hell are these masks? Gross!

00:30.840 --> 00:32.670
We all have them on.

00:32.670 --> 00:34.130
<i>Careful with those.</i>

00:35.050 --> 00:38.140
<i>If you forcefully take them off,
they'll explode.</i>

00:38.300 --> 00:40.390
- What the hell?
- Who're you?

00:40.390 --> 00:44.390
<i>My name is Jig-Jag. Play a game with me.</i>

00:45.060 --> 00:46.850
Hey, this is...

00:46.850 --> 00:47.770
Yeah.

00:47.940 --> 00:53.360
A strange mask, a modulated deep voice,
and orders from a monitor...

00:53.990 --> 00:56.490
<i>We're trapped in a death game!</i>

02:27.910 --> 02:29.250
You gotta be kidding me!

02:29.540 --> 02:31.630
Why the hell do we have to do this?

02:31.790 --> 02:36.460
<i>I just want to play a game.
But with serious risks!</i>

02:37.010 --> 02:40.130
<i>And that's why I chose the four of you.</i>

02:40.300 --> 02:43.010
<i>Especially since I have her
as a hostage.</i>

02:43.180 --> 02:44.140
Nico!

02:44.260 --> 02:46.810
<i>I'm sorry everyone. I got caught.</i>

02:46.810 --> 02:48.770
<i>We're in a different room.</i>

02:48.890 --> 02:54.480
If you disobey my orders
or attempt to destroy the building,

02:54.480 --> 02:56.780
your masks will explode.

02:56.900 --> 03:00.030
Of course, her life
will become forfeit as well.

03:01.570 --> 03:02.530
All right.

03:02.740 --> 03:06.870
If you promise to release Nico,
we'll play along with whatever you want.

03:08.040 --> 03:09.660
<i>I'm glad you understand.</i>

03:10.160 --> 03:13.670
<i>The game that I have created
for you to play is called...</i>

03:14.540 --> 03:16.210
<i>Ouroboros.</i>

03:16.210 --> 03:17.380
Ouroboros?

03:17.380 --> 03:19.920
It's the symbol that shows a snake
eating its own tail.

03:20.130 --> 03:22.470
<i>Whispering or casual talk is not allowed.</i>

03:22.470 --> 03:24.550
<i>I will be giving all the orders.</i>

03:24.890 --> 03:29.680
<i>You will all be snakes, so I shall grant you
the names of snake gods.</i>

03:29.680 --> 03:32.020
<i>Morihito Otogi shall be Apophis.</i>

03:32.140 --> 03:34.690
<i>Kanshi Kazamatsuri shall be Illuyanka.</i>

03:34.810 --> 03:36.900
<i>Keigo Magami shall be Naga.</i>

03:36.900 --> 03:38.570
<i>Miharu Kiryu shall be Python.</i>

03:38.780 --> 03:41.030
<i>There are squares drawn on the floor.</i>

03:41.030 --> 03:44.110
<i>Each of you will stand in a corner
and we'll begin.</i>

03:44.530 --> 03:48.620
<i>I've installed an original dice app
into your phones.</i>

03:48.620 --> 03:51.370
<i>I can see your dice rolls as well.</i>

03:51.660 --> 03:55.920
<i>Within the game, we will refer to the dice
as "vice," which represents evil.</i>

03:55.920 --> 03:59.880
<i>There are nine types of vice,
so pick one before you roll.</i>

04:00.380 --> 04:02.630
<i>The normal vice.</i>

04:02.760 --> 04:05.140
<i>The even vice with only even numbers.</i>

04:05.430 --> 04:07.720
<i>The odd vice with only odd numbers.</i>

04:07.890 --> 04:11.730
<i>The ace vice has ones on three sides,
which increases the odds of rolling a one.</i>

04:11.730 --> 04:14.770
<i>In the same fashion, the deuce vice
increases the odds of rolling a two.</i>

04:14.770 --> 04:17.360
<i>The trey vice increases the odds
of rolling a three.</i>

04:17.360 --> 04:19.860
<i>The cater vice increases the odds
of rolling a four.</i>

04:19.860 --> 04:22.360
<i>The cinque vice increases the odds
of rolling a five.</i>

04:22.360 --> 04:24.660
<i>And the sice vice increases the odds
of rolling a six.</i>

04:25.610 --> 04:29.490
<i>When I say, "Roll the vice,"
everyone will roll the vice they picked</i>

04:29.490 --> 04:31.410
<i>and move forward that many squares.</i>

04:32.040 --> 04:35.170
<i>There are nine squares on each side,
and you'll move counterclockwise.</i>

04:35.540 --> 04:38.170
<i>Once a player lands
on another player's square,</i>

04:38.170 --> 04:43.300
<i>it means that a snake has eaten another snake,
and the eaten snake is removed.</i>

04:43.970 --> 04:48.140
<i>It's snakes chasing and being chased,
and you fight to nom or get nommed.</i>

04:48.140 --> 04:52.640
<i>I wanted to play this game with
the four of you, who share a deep bond.</i>

04:54.600 --> 04:56.940
<i>Let me explain the symbols
on the squares.</i>

04:57.100 --> 05:01.530
<i>If you land on the square with the plus sign,
you coil up and skip a turn.</i>

05:01.780 --> 05:04.490
<i>If you land on a triangle,
then you become a reverse snake,</i>

05:04.490 --> 05:06.570
<i>and move the opposite way.</i>

05:06.950 --> 05:10.330
<i>The fifth square on each side has a cross bridge,
which lets you cross sides.</i>

05:10.330 --> 05:12.500
<i>You can choose
to take that path or not.</i>

05:12.500 --> 05:13.700
<i>The cross bridge utilizes</i>

05:13.700 --> 05:16.620
<i>the middle of the board as one square,
and so with two...</i>

05:16.620 --> 05:18.830
<i>This is taking forever.</i>

05:19.080 --> 05:20.880
<i>Okay, let's start!</i>

05:20.880 --> 05:23.710
I feel like there's still
some gaps in the rules.

05:23.710 --> 05:26.800
<i>No talking! Now, roll the vice!</i>

05:27.840 --> 05:28.840
APOPHIS

05:30.100 --> 05:31.100
ILLUYANKA

05:32.350 --> 05:33.350
NAGA

05:34.480 --> 05:35.480
PYTHON

05:38.650 --> 05:40.980
<i>Dang, I have to skip my next turn.</i>

05:41.520 --> 05:43.780
<i>So Kanshi has to skip
his next turn, huh?</i>

05:43.900 --> 05:46.150
<i>Ugh, you don't even need
a strategy for this game.</i>

05:46.150 --> 05:48.450
<i>You can just pick the vice
with the sixes.</i>

05:48.610 --> 05:51.200
<i>Turn two! Roll the vice!</i>

05:52.280 --> 05:53.240
<i>There's my six.</i>

05:52.950 --> 05:56.330
APOPHIS

05:55.120 --> 05:59.170
One, two, three, four, five...

05:59.540 --> 06:03.340
Wait, what? Did I just... get... eaten?

06:10.180 --> 06:12.300
What the hell,
this game ain't fun at all!

06:12.300 --> 06:13.810
It's over in just two turns!

06:12.300 --> 06:19.560
WE GOT TRAPPED IN A DEATH GAME, BUT IT SUCKED

06:13.810 --> 06:17.270
<i>No, that was just...
You guys got really lucky.</i>

06:17.270 --> 06:20.150
No it's not, it happened naturally!
These rules are bonkers!

06:20.520 --> 06:21.730
What a dumb game.

06:21.730 --> 06:24.650
What do you mean Ouroboros?
More like Ouro-boring!

06:25.030 --> 06:27.360
The explanation is too long,
there are too many rules,

06:27.360 --> 06:29.490
and once we started playing, I got eaten?

06:29.490 --> 06:31.160
Or should I say I got nommed?

06:31.160 --> 06:34.160
Everything was serious, so I couldn't
say anything, but now I don't care!

06:34.370 --> 06:37.830
If you're gonna trap us in a death game,
make sure it's fun!

06:39.250 --> 06:41.290
What're you gonna do now?
You kidnapped five of us!

06:41.290 --> 06:45.170
You say, "Let's play a game," in a deep voice,
but I can't take you seriously anymore!

06:45.550 --> 06:47.300
Um, Mr. Zigzag?

06:47.300 --> 06:48.420
<i>It's Jig-Jag.</i>

06:48.420 --> 06:52.300
Do you mind if we streamline
the rules so they're understandable?

06:52.510 --> 06:54.140
<i>Aww, but...</i>

06:54.140 --> 06:58.520
Even if you don't want to, this game is stupidly
boring and isn't even a real game yet.

06:58.520 --> 07:00.520
You shouldn't be proud of that.

07:00.520 --> 07:01.810
Maybe you should go easy on him.

07:01.900 --> 07:05.320
I'm just saying we should all take
this chance to make it more fun.

07:07.780 --> 07:08.860
<i>All right, go ahead.</i>

07:08.860 --> 07:10.650
How's it gotta feel to say that?

07:10.650 --> 07:14.280
<i>And so, the meeting to improve
Ouroboros has begun.</i>

07:11.410 --> 07:12.660
OUROBOROS REVISION MEETING

07:14.530 --> 07:17.040
First, let's get rid of the things
that aren't necessary.

07:17.040 --> 07:20.540
I agree. We don't need snake god names,
and one dice is enough!

07:20.540 --> 07:21.670
<i>Wait, really?</i>

07:21.670 --> 07:23.500
I want to get rid of the reverse snake.

07:23.500 --> 07:24.540
<i>That, too?</i>

07:24.920 --> 07:28.460
In a "nom or get nommed" game, if you're
moving forward and backward,

07:28.460 --> 07:31.970
then two heads would eventually clash,
and I felt uneasy about that.

07:31.970 --> 07:34.300
In a game of Ouroboros,
the head should nom on the tail.

07:34.300 --> 07:37.310
It's funny how the term
"nom" stuck with us.

07:37.640 --> 07:41.640
If we all just moved in one direction,
the flow would become easier,

07:41.640 --> 07:45.020
and the concept of Ouroboros
chasing its tail can be preserved.

07:45.310 --> 07:46.320
Amazing!

07:46.320 --> 07:49.690
You're the only one wanting to preserve
the concept of the game.

07:50.110 --> 07:51.780
<i>I think I'm gonna cry.</i>

07:51.780 --> 07:55.320
Furthermore, I'd like to change
this game's greatest weakness.

07:55.490 --> 07:58.700
It's when a player reaches another
player's square, and must nom them.

07:59.120 --> 08:00.700
Earlier, I rolled a six.

08:01.000 --> 08:02.960
On the fifth square, I had to nom Kanshi.

08:03.210 --> 08:06.630
We should change the rules so that
I can only nom him if I roll an exact five!

08:06.630 --> 08:07.920
I like it!

08:07.920 --> 08:10.880
Whatever movements are left,
the player should pass the other player.

08:10.880 --> 08:14.970
Then, the chaser becomes
the one being chased!

08:18.010 --> 08:19.430
<i>And so...</i>

08:19.430 --> 08:22.940
Okay, I'd like to announce
the new rules for Ouroboros.

08:23.140 --> 08:24.850
My plan has already...

08:25.020 --> 08:28.110
First, each player will use coins
to represent themselves.

08:28.110 --> 08:29.940
<i>It became a board game!</i>

08:29.940 --> 08:31.900
There's one type of dice
and we take turns.

08:32.240 --> 08:33.530
A warp has been added in.

08:33.530 --> 08:36.910
If you stop at a corner, you can choose
to teleport yourself across the board.

08:36.910 --> 08:38.910
<i>It's anything goes now, isn't it?</i>

08:38.910 --> 08:42.790
And then, if a snake noms on another snake,
you can stack the coins like so...

08:42.790 --> 08:44.120
and become a twin-headed snake!

08:44.120 --> 08:45.670
<i>What's that awesome-looking thing?</i>

08:45.670 --> 08:48.420
The twin-headed snake's movement speed
is double the number on the dice.

08:48.590 --> 08:51.300
- Three heads means three times the speed.
<i>- Wait, a power up?</i>

08:51.590 --> 08:54.340
<i>With these rules, even though
the number of players decrease,</i>

08:54.340 --> 08:58.220
<i>the game can still be speedy and thrilling
without reaching a stalemate.</i>

08:58.220 --> 09:00.060
I believed in you guys!

09:00.390 --> 09:01.890
Let's try playing it!

09:01.890 --> 09:04.020
<i>Yeah, let's play! Roll the vice!</i>

09:04.020 --> 09:05.600
We don't need
that dumb callout anymore.

09:05.600 --> 09:06.940
What? Dumb?

09:07.480 --> 09:10.320
Wait, why were we doing this
in the first place?

09:10.520 --> 09:14.900
Oh, that's right.
Nico got caught, and... Huh?

09:14.900 --> 09:16.450
Wait, Nico?

09:16.450 --> 09:18.700
I wanna play with you guys, too.

09:18.870 --> 09:20.780
Huh? What's going on?

09:20.870 --> 09:22.910
Nico was an accomplice, too.

09:23.540 --> 09:27.880
You're a magic user, yet you were
only restrained with a single rope.

09:29.210 --> 09:32.340
And who else could have put
the four of us to sleep and moved us

09:32.340 --> 09:34.050
all at once by themselves?

09:34.050 --> 09:35.720
You noticed all that?

09:36.010 --> 09:39.850
I'm sorry I tricked you,
but I was asked for help, so...

09:39.970 --> 09:42.180
Asked for help? By who?

09:42.180 --> 09:44.640
There's one among us
who hasn't spoken a single word yet.

09:49.520 --> 09:50.730
Whoa, what the...

09:51.110 --> 09:55.110
I used the Doppelganger spell
to create another Keigo.

09:55.110 --> 09:58.200
Another one? Then the real one is...

09:58.280 --> 09:59.410
It's you!

09:59.410 --> 10:01.160
<i>Sorry I tricked you.</i>

10:01.160 --> 10:05.750
<i>I wanted to go viral, so I was trying
to record an "I tried a death game" video.</i>

10:05.870 --> 10:08.620
Now that I look,
there are hidden cameras everywhere.

10:08.830 --> 10:10.630
The idea seems fun,

10:10.630 --> 10:13.590
but the game itself is craptastically boring,
so there's no way it'll go viral.

10:13.590 --> 10:14.880
Please go easy on him.

10:15.130 --> 10:17.380
<i>I wonder if I'm not good at this stuff.</i>

10:17.550 --> 10:21.680
You should've realized that when you made
grasshoppers sumo wrestle on a slippery surface.

10:21.680 --> 10:25.020
I TRAPPED THEM IN A DEATH GAME,
BUT THEY TOTALLY FIXED IT

10:21.930 --> 10:23.930
<i>But it went viral after all!</i>

10:39.570 --> 10:42.200
Kazamatsuri is the descendant
of a tengu.

10:42.200 --> 10:44.290
Magami is a werewolf.

10:44.290 --> 10:46.040
And there's also
a vampire at your house.

10:46.580 --> 10:48.250
It's like a haunted house.

10:48.250 --> 10:49.330
We get that a lot.

10:49.870 --> 10:52.710
It seems like a portion of the students
know your true identity,

10:52.710 --> 10:54.210
but how's your school life been?

10:54.500 --> 10:58.920
I've opened up to friends I trust,
and they're all cool with it.

10:58.920 --> 11:02.680
Nico's status as a witch is too powerful,
so we aren't that exciting by comparison.

11:02.680 --> 11:06.020
Yeah, everyone thinks that having
a tengu around isn't that strange.

11:06.020 --> 11:07.310
I see.

11:07.310 --> 11:10.850
If something happens, please come
talk to me. That's all for today.

11:10.850 --> 11:12.730
Oh, that was the whole meeting?

11:12.730 --> 11:15.610
Yes. Can you sign here,
acknowledging that we finished?

11:15.610 --> 11:18.110
Oh, the pencil's kinda short.

11:18.650 --> 11:19.820
Here's another one.

11:19.820 --> 11:23.370
It's okay, I'd like to show you my magic.

11:23.530 --> 11:25.410
Enlongen!

11:28.660 --> 11:29.500
That's strange.

11:29.660 --> 11:32.210
I just learned it,
so I might've messed up.

11:32.210 --> 11:34.500
I wanted to make the pencil longer.

11:34.500 --> 11:36.800
You don't need to use your magic
on such trivial things.

11:37.920 --> 11:39.670
Nico, are you done?

11:39.970 --> 11:44.760
Yeah! Moi, I'm gonna go with Kara and Kuku,
so don't worry about guarding me.

11:44.760 --> 11:45.600
All right.

11:46.100 --> 11:48.270
Hey, wanna drop by somewhere
real quick?

11:48.270 --> 11:50.770
- Sure! Where do you wanna go?
- Sounds good, maybe to a diner?

11:52.230 --> 11:54.360
There's actually something
I need to talk about.

11:55.900 --> 11:57.360
A few teachers have spoken up

11:57.360 --> 12:01.740
and requested that all of you be placed
under special surveillance.

12:01.950 --> 12:03.320
Special surveillance?

12:03.660 --> 12:05.870
It's a proposal where you'll be registered

12:05.870 --> 12:09.040
as dangerous students and
will have to periodically report to us.

12:09.040 --> 12:11.830
Hold on a second, what do you mean
dangerous? We're just...

12:11.830 --> 12:13.080
I understand.

12:13.290 --> 12:17.590
However, Nico Wakatsuki's magic
has been the cause of several incidents.

12:17.590 --> 12:19.090
Though it was another personality,

12:19.090 --> 12:22.800
Magami was the mastermind behind
the student brainwashing incident.

12:24.090 --> 12:27.010
Please understand why the teachers
are being cautious.

12:27.220 --> 12:31.020
For now, the teachers are waiting
for my investigation results.

12:31.230 --> 12:36.480
Please try not to cause any disturbances,
especially incidents relating to magic.

12:36.810 --> 12:38.360
- Okay.
- Understood.

12:38.360 --> 12:39.610
All right.

12:40.860 --> 12:42.950
Wh-What in the world is that?

12:42.950 --> 12:46.990
Huh? What? My point of view is...
Did I suddenly grow taller?

12:46.990 --> 12:49.580
Your neck! Your neck has gotten longer!

12:49.580 --> 12:50.830
And your nails!

12:50.830 --> 12:53.250
Whoa, you're right!
My nails have gotten longer!

12:53.540 --> 12:55.500
What's going on?

12:58.250 --> 13:00.000
My hair suddenly grew!

13:00.210 --> 13:03.470
This phenomenon must be magic!
That means...

13:03.720 --> 13:05.430
President, your right arm...

13:05.430 --> 13:07.680
MULTIPURPOSE ROOM

13:06.220 --> 13:10.310
The spell that Nico just used, Enlongen,
is closely related to Embiggen.

13:10.640 --> 13:14.690
If it was emitted from her fingertips,
then it gets cast on one part of the target.

13:15.060 --> 13:17.190
I don't think she spread
her thumb out far enough,

13:17.190 --> 13:20.320
so the spell might've been emitted
from her four fingers.

13:20.610 --> 13:24.450
The delayed activation might be because
of her inexperience with that spell.

13:24.700 --> 13:27.160
Impressive observational skills, Otogi.

13:27.160 --> 13:28.450
I have experience with this.

13:28.660 --> 13:30.620
So, as I was trying to say before,

13:30.620 --> 13:34.960
I asked you not to create
any commotion relating to magic.

13:35.120 --> 13:37.330
We're really sorry about this.

13:37.330 --> 13:39.840
This will be bad if the teachers
see us like this.

13:39.960 --> 13:41.840
How do we get back to normal?

13:41.840 --> 13:45.590
If the same spell is cast on the elongated part,
it should go back to normal.

13:45.590 --> 13:47.800
But we can't go anywhere
looking like this.

13:47.930 --> 13:50.850
We'll have to configure this
so we look more normal.

13:50.850 --> 13:52.390
Why're you posed like that?

13:52.390 --> 13:54.480
If I don't do this, I'll get slashed up!

13:55.020 --> 13:58.600
Morihito looks like a horror-themed
visual kei band member,

13:58.600 --> 14:01.770
so if you say you're a guy
who looks up to Vega, it'll work.

14:02.070 --> 14:04.820
Keigo doesn't even look human at all.

14:04.820 --> 14:07.150
Can't we say
this is just the kind of creature he is?

14:07.150 --> 14:08.780
What kind of creature is that?

14:09.070 --> 14:11.280
The real problem
is Team Long Limbs here.

14:11.280 --> 14:13.040
You both look like yokai.

14:13.370 --> 14:16.410
Looks like we don't have to worry
about joints in the elongated parts.

14:16.410 --> 14:18.120
Yeah, it's pretty squishy.

14:18.120 --> 14:19.170
If that's the case...

14:19.540 --> 14:20.960
You can wrap it around, like so.

14:20.960 --> 14:22.290
Oh, I think that kinda works?

14:22.290 --> 14:24.420
How could you say that? My neck is fat!

14:24.590 --> 14:26.720
Actually, there's a pro wrestler
who looks like that.

14:26.720 --> 14:29.260
Do I look like I have the body
of a wrestler to you?

14:29.260 --> 14:32.640
It's unnatural for my body to be super thin
and my neck to be super fat.

14:32.810 --> 14:34.970
And there's some weird layering
going on, too.

14:34.970 --> 14:37.350
We can just say that
your fat is hanging, right?

14:37.350 --> 14:39.690
The Witch of the Waste
looks something like that, too.

14:39.690 --> 14:41.860
What happened
to the pro wrestler backstory?

14:42.190 --> 14:46.360
That's a trivial problem.
The real problem is...

14:48.110 --> 14:49.200
Your arm, huh?

14:49.200 --> 14:51.160
Why such a grievous face?

14:51.320 --> 14:55.490
Okay, well, let's try wrapping your arm
around your body.

14:55.740 --> 14:57.000
All right.

14:59.830 --> 15:02.630
- No, that doesn't seem possible.
- Please let go of your hat!

15:02.630 --> 15:06.380
Besides, why are you so hung up
on never letting go of your hat?

15:06.380 --> 15:09.970
I'm just expressing myself
in my own personal way.

15:09.970 --> 15:12.140
Do you really have to do that right now?

15:12.140 --> 15:13.390
Then, I shall take off my hat.

15:13.390 --> 15:15.310
So, it looks like that part didn't matter.

15:15.310 --> 15:17.680
And then, you just wrap it
around your body.

15:19.060 --> 15:20.350
It looks like a sash now.

15:20.350 --> 15:22.100
It doesn't feel as weird as I thought.

15:22.100 --> 15:24.150
Is your sense of judgement sinking?

15:24.400 --> 15:26.780
How about we just put a sash over it?

15:28.110 --> 15:29.360
I AM THE STUDENT COUNCIL PRESIDENT

15:28.570 --> 15:29.360
Please, no!

15:29.530 --> 15:32.240
Nah, you look great!
It's giving student council president.

15:32.240 --> 15:34.070
I am the Student Council President!

15:34.070 --> 15:38.250
What Student Council President goes
around wearing a sash that proclaims it?

15:38.580 --> 15:40.000
But your arm's kinda short here.

15:41.580 --> 15:44.080
A little oddness is fine at this point.

15:44.080 --> 15:45.750
I mean, could you just let go?

15:45.840 --> 15:48.010
You have to tilt your neck
to set your head on your hat.

15:48.010 --> 15:50.050
That looks way more odd.

15:50.050 --> 15:52.340
Hey! What's going on in here?

15:52.340 --> 15:53.550
Oh shoot, it's a teacher.

15:53.550 --> 15:54.600
What should we do?

15:54.600 --> 15:56.640
Otogi, you have to talk to him.

15:59.730 --> 16:02.230
N-Nothing much.

16:02.850 --> 16:05.440
Otogi? What happened to your nails?

16:05.440 --> 16:08.320
Oh, um, this is...

16:08.480 --> 16:12.450
I-I was gonna debut in a visual kei band
that had Vega vibes, and...

16:12.450 --> 16:15.070
Wh-What language are you speaking?

16:16.370 --> 16:18.160
Is there someone behind you?

16:18.620 --> 16:20.790
O-Oh hello there, Mr. Minechi.

16:21.000 --> 16:24.750
Oh, it's you, Kiyomiya. Huh? Wait!

16:25.080 --> 16:26.540
What happened to your neck?

16:26.540 --> 16:28.380
My neck? Oh, yes, my neck.

16:28.380 --> 16:32.090
I, um, slept a little strangely last night
so I'm doing this to not be in pain.

16:32.090 --> 16:36.180
I see, hard working as always.
Don't overexert yourself, okay?

16:37.100 --> 16:39.100
And you over there...

16:39.560 --> 16:40.680
Whazzup!

16:40.680 --> 16:44.480
See here, I'm trying to become a pro wrestler!
The name's Necktie Wastewitch, hur!

16:44.480 --> 16:46.980
Wastewitch? Do we have such a student?

16:47.150 --> 16:51.190
I was just guiding Otogi and Wastewitch
on their daily life demeanor.

16:51.190 --> 16:54.360
I see. Spirited as always,
and you even got a sash.

16:54.360 --> 16:57.490
We're very proud of you.
Don't get too rowdy, okay?

16:57.490 --> 16:59.120
Of course. We're terribly sorry.

16:59.120 --> 17:00.580
Yeah, our bad.

17:00.580 --> 17:02.910
We'll be careful, hur.

17:03.660 --> 17:05.370
<i>He didn't notice me.</i>

17:05.670 --> 17:07.500
Hey, we did a good job fooling him.

17:07.500 --> 17:09.340
Perhaps this can work after all.

17:09.340 --> 17:11.630
Okay, let's head to my house.

17:13.420 --> 17:17.090
But I doubt we'll make it all the way there
without bumping into someone.

17:17.090 --> 17:18.890
What's the plan when we do?

17:19.810 --> 17:21.640
And I see a classmate already.

17:21.930 --> 17:23.480
Hide in my blind spot.

17:24.390 --> 17:25.770
<i>If we run into anyone...</i>

17:25.770 --> 17:26.900
Hey, Otogi.

17:27.150 --> 17:28.900
<i>...we'll trick them by going too fast!</i>

17:28.900 --> 17:29.820
See ya later!

17:29.820 --> 17:31.480
Yeah, later.

17:32.110 --> 17:33.650
Wow, that really worked.

17:34.950 --> 17:37.700
<i>No, it wasn't just speed.</i>

17:38.120 --> 17:42.790
<i>By continuously pointing his nails straight
at the person, he disguised the length.</i>

17:42.790 --> 17:45.460
<i>As they say,
a skilled hawk hides its talons!</i>

17:46.040 --> 17:50.710
<i>Accurate situational awareness, quick action,
and precise bodily movements.</i>

17:52.250 --> 17:55.420
I would really like for you
to join the Student Council, Otogi!

17:55.420 --> 17:56.430
President!

17:56.430 --> 17:59.550
Would you keep moving?
We're in a hurry!

18:01.430 --> 18:02.770
What the hell?

18:05.890 --> 18:08.190
President unwound
like a spinning top!

18:08.190 --> 18:09.520
Don't pull too hard!

18:09.520 --> 18:11.900
It was so natural
that I had almost forgotten,

18:11.900 --> 18:14.030
but my arm is wrapped around my body.

18:14.030 --> 18:17.860
No, it's totally not natural.
But, I'm sorry. I acted brashly.

18:18.320 --> 18:21.490
Well, I'm glad
there aren't that many people around.

18:21.490 --> 18:24.160
As long as we don't move around
in a weird way, we should be okay.

18:24.160 --> 18:28.120
Be careful Kanshi, your neck
is like a spring right now.

18:28.120 --> 18:29.670
If you jump too high...

18:30.080 --> 18:31.040
You see?

18:31.040 --> 18:33.340
Put it back before anyone sees!

18:33.340 --> 18:34.630
Sorry, guys.

18:38.090 --> 18:39.260
What's wrong?

18:39.260 --> 18:43.180
I don't know.
I can't feel anything below my knees.

18:43.180 --> 18:45.270
- You got lightheaded.
- Lightheaded?

18:45.270 --> 18:47.020
ORTHOSTATIC HYPOTENSION

18:45.680 --> 18:47.020
Orthostatic hypotension​.

18:47.770 --> 18:50.270
When you stand up too fast
from a low crouch,

18:50.480 --> 18:53.520
you get dizzy for a second because
there isn't enough blood going to your brain.

18:53.650 --> 18:56.530
Because Kanshi's neck is so long,
the difference in elevation was too much.

18:56.530 --> 18:58.530
What's with this realistic health hazard?

18:58.780 --> 19:00.950
A-Am I gonna die?

19:00.950 --> 19:04.160
You're just feeling a bit dizzy!
Please don't cry when you look like that.

19:04.290 --> 19:06.040
Wh-What is it?

19:06.040 --> 19:08.210
Magami. Become my cape.

19:08.210 --> 19:09.670
What? Your cape?

19:10.040 --> 19:13.000
My back looks quite disgustingly squishy
and it's gross.

19:13.090 --> 19:15.170
And you are entirely gross.

19:15.300 --> 19:18.510
What I'm saying is that we shall
complement each other's grossness.

19:18.510 --> 19:21.260
That sounds like quite
the gross win-win situation.

19:27.980 --> 19:29.390
I'm gonna throw up!

19:29.390 --> 19:30.690
That's no cape!

19:30.690 --> 19:33.400
You just look like a military man
who got possessed by a monster!

19:33.770 --> 19:36.570
I was imagining
a raggedy, old, cool-looking cape.

19:36.570 --> 19:38.740
No way, man.
That's definitely a mino straw raincoat.

19:38.860 --> 19:40.490
Someone help me!

19:40.780 --> 19:42.240
Did you hear something?

19:42.240 --> 19:43.660
Someone needs help.

19:43.660 --> 19:44.450
Where?

19:44.620 --> 19:46.200
All right!

19:47.750 --> 19:50.710
H-Hey, stop. What if someone sees us?

19:50.710 --> 19:52.250
There's no time for that.

19:53.460 --> 19:56.210
Over there! A guy's dangling by a rope!

19:56.590 --> 19:57.510
Let's go, Keigo.

19:57.510 --> 19:58.210
Okay!

20:05.680 --> 20:06.390
Catch him!

20:10.810 --> 20:15.150
I mean, just because my hair is long
doesn't mean I have extra cushioning.

20:16.150 --> 20:18.230
Oh wow, thank you.

20:18.230 --> 20:20.900
I was fixing my roof
when I suddenly slipped and...

20:20.900 --> 20:23.030
Oh my god! What are you guys?

20:23.450 --> 20:24.660
I'm an ogre.

20:24.660 --> 20:25.830
I'm a tengu.

20:25.830 --> 20:27.160
I'm a werewolf.

20:29.160 --> 20:30.910
We're glad you're not hurt.

20:33.710 --> 20:37.380
<i>Are they not afraid to be seen
with judging eyes?</i>

20:40.880 --> 20:41.920
Watch out!

20:46.850 --> 20:48.640
My apologies for frightening you.

20:48.970 --> 20:53.850
A-An ogre, a tengu,
a werewolf, and you're...

20:54.900 --> 20:56.690
Student Council President?

21:05.030 --> 21:06.740
W-We made it.

21:07.160 --> 21:08.830
Regarding what we talked about earlier...

21:08.830 --> 21:11.370
I shall decline
the special surveillance request.

21:11.370 --> 21:12.500
Really?

21:12.500 --> 21:15.420
Yes. We'll continue the regular check-ins,

21:15.420 --> 21:18.170
but I've decided that nothing further
needs to be done.

21:22.170 --> 21:26.390
Even though you are feared, you were fearless
when it came to extending a helping hand.

21:26.390 --> 21:28.260
You've taught me something as well.

21:29.680 --> 21:32.520
Plus, I really don't care about
other people's opinions about me.

21:33.600 --> 21:36.650
Our students are pretty open-minded
about weird things.

21:36.810 --> 21:39.270
I don't think anyone's afraid of us.

21:40.900 --> 21:41.780
Hey, now!

21:41.780 --> 21:43.530
This is your fault.

21:43.530 --> 21:46.740
Oh, I see.
Let me dispel that Enlongen.

21:46.990 --> 21:49.240
This is progressing strangely well.

21:49.240 --> 21:51.580
It's like a daily thing for us.

21:52.450 --> 21:55.290
I'd like you to be in the same position
when the spell was cast,

21:55.290 --> 21:57.120
so the four of you, please line up.

21:57.330 --> 21:59.130
Why are you guys here, too?

21:59.130 --> 22:01.130
Because it sounds like fun.

22:02.710 --> 22:05.010
Enlongen!

22:10.930 --> 22:12.770
It's all long now!

22:13.020 --> 22:14.890
Oh no, looks like I missed.

22:14.890 --> 22:17.100
Why am I the only one who got hit twice?

22:17.100 --> 22:19.100
I'm so sorry!

23:57.660 --> 24:00.040
How long am I gonna
look like Captain Kuro?

24:00.040 --> 24:02.670
And my nose looks like Usopp's nose.

24:02.670 --> 24:05.250
It's my two front teeth for me!
Am I from Game Center Arashi or something?

24:04.960 --> 24:12.010
NEXT EPISODE
KARA AND SHIKI
MEGA MARBLE MANIA MADNESS
SCRAMBLE SCRAP SQUAD

24:05.250 --> 24:08.130
I am Maetel, the woman who traverses
through the flow of time.

24:08.130 --> 24:12.010
Oh, um, uh, I can't think of a character
who has a long chin and neck!
